# Execution targets

Optional sealed-packet field `execution_target` (not one of the required seven).
Tokens: `worktree` (omitted/empty default), `isolated_copy`, `openshell:<name>`,
`cloud_subagent`. Unknown tokens fail closed — not coerced.

`openshell:<name>` matches `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,62}$`. Reserved names `hermes`,
`pi`, `eval` are illegal as the name and as `program.site_path`. Never
`openshell sandbox connect --editor cursor`. Never put app source in those
reserved sandboxes.

Corporate roles stay `worktree`. site-specialist defaults to
`.worktrees/<packet-id>`. operations-excellence and site adversary
`independent_review` require `isolated_copy` (oracle tree ≠ implementer tree)
and do not follow into OpenShell or `cloud_subagent`.

A green sandbox/VM/worktree is not a named-gate PASS. Oracles remain
`scripts/harness/{verify,adversarial}.sh`. Agents never `--actor user`.
No corp-harness sandbox/VM runtime.
